# Authors of Núcleo

Sergio Iván Ullaguari Alvarado <security@nucleoledger.com>

This is the author of every commit in the repository's history but one: commit
`b894337` (2026-10-09) is a dependency bump authored by `dependabot[bot]`, merged
by the author through GitHub's web interface in `5237867`, which records the author as
"Sergio Ullaguari" with a GitHub no-reply address.

Since 2026-10-02 the author commits as the identity above. Commits made before
2026-10-02 (from 2026-09-03 to 2026-09-28) record the same person under the short
name "Sergio U" and a different, personal e-mail address. The history is left as
it is: rewriting it would change every commit hash after the first one, including
those named by the published release tags.

What is signed, exactly: **commits are not**. The two that carry a signature,
`b894337` and `5237867`, were signed by GitHub, not by the author. The tags
`v0.3.0-alpha`, `v0.3.1-alpha`, `vsdk-0.3.0-alpha.0` and `vsdk-0.4.0-alpha.0` are
signed with the author's SSH key as the identity above (`git tag -v`); the earlier
tags `v0.1.0-alpha`, `v0.2.0-alpha` and `vsdk-0.2.0-alpha.0` are annotated but not
signed. The release binaries are signed separately, keyless, by the release
workflow (see `docs/RELEASING.md`).

Most commits also carry a `Co-Authored-By:` trailer naming an AI model (Claude,
by Anthropic), which the author used to write code and documentation. This file
records that fact as it appears in the history; it does not state what it means
for authorship or ownership.
